message: "If you use pkpdsim, please cite it as below."
title: "pkpdsim: building blocks of physiologically based pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic models in SBML"
abstract: "pkpdsim is a library for physiologically based pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic (PBPK/PD) models in SBML: a standard physiology at its centre, the substances, chemistry, routes and observers of a model on top of it, and the simulation experiments, fits, scans, uncertainty and credibility of sbmlsim on top of those. The physiology is the organs of ICRP 89 with their volumes, blood flows and blood, scaled to the individual of a study and changed by its condition, with the laboratory species, virtual populations, impaired liver, kidney and cardiac function, pregnancy, circadian rhythms, the adipose tissue, the standard organ and its variants, among them the zonated liver and the circuit of an ex vivo machine perfusion. The building blocks are what a model writes on top of it: one definition of its substances with their mechanism flags, the chemistry of its organs, its routes and its observers, which the library builds into the SBML, a comp model with one submodel per organ and the flat model which is simulated, annotated and with every number carrying the publication it is taken from. The analysis is the capabilities of sbmlsim in the PBPK context: the published studies of a model as simulation experiments with a shared vocabulary of their metadata, the fits with their uncertainty, the scans and sensitivity analyses, the assessment of the contexts of use of a model, the commands which work with every model package and the release of a model as a repository of its own."
